# {{.Title}}

Created with `gortisan create`. Every file here belongs to this project: nothing
imports gortisan, and gortisan is not in `go.mod`. Change anything.

## Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env
./gortisan run               # builds cmd/api, runs it, restarts on every change
                             # (or: go run ./cmd/api)
curl localhost:8000/ping     # {"ping":"pong"}
curl localhost:8000/health   # {"status":"pass","checks":{...}}

```


## Layout

```
cmd/api/main.go           builds every dependency in order and starts the HTTP service
internal/
  domain/                 the business — no HTTP, no Kafka
    user/                 one package per subject; group them when there are many (sales/order)
      user.go             the struct — the table, with bun tags
      errors.go           failures in business terms (ErrNotFound…)
      store.go            what the service needs from storage
      repository.go       implements the store on orm.Repository (bun)
      service.go          the rules — what the API and workers call
  api/                    HTTP
    router.go             /ping, /health, and one line per API version
    v1/routes.go          every v1 endpoint
    v1/users/           handler.go, request.go (inputs), response.go (outputs)

  platform/               infrastructure — no business rules
    config/ server/ validate/ problem/ health/
    trans/lang/fa.json    every text the API shows, by key
{{- if .Postgres}}
    database/             opens the database from the config
    database/orm/         bun over pgx: Repository[T], scopes, relations, transactions
{{- end}}
{{- if .Redis}}
    cache/
{{- end}}

tests/
  arch_test.go            fails `go test` when a layer imports the wrong way
```

Dependencies point one way — `api` → `domain` → `platform` —
and `tests/arch_test.go` enforces it, including that `api/v2` never imports
`api/v1`.

## Rules

- **Dependencies are passed, not looked up.** Constructors take what they need;
  `cmd/api/main.go` wires them. No globals, no values hidden in `context.Context`.
- **The domain names its errors** (`user.ErrNotFound`); the handler decides the
  HTTP status. Any other error becomes a 500 and is logged.
- **Validation:** a validator in `internal/api/validator/<group>/` (make:validator)
  either stops the request (`address.NewMobile("body.mobile", m).Validate(ctx)`) or
  joins the others (`errs.Check(ctx, ...)`, `errs.Add(...)`, `return errs.Err()`).
- **Errors are RFC 9457 problem details** (`application/problem+json`), and every
  text is a key of `internal/platform/trans/lang/fa.json`: `trans.Message("general:entity-not-found", "سفارش")`.
{{- if .Postgres}}
- **Transactions are explicit.** `orm.InTx(ctx, db, func(ctx context.Context, tx orm.IDB) error { ... })`
  and `repo.WithTx(tx)`.

## The database layer

A model is a struct with bun tags ([bun](https://bun.uptrace.dev) over pgx):

```go
type Invoice struct {
	bun.BaseModel `bun:"table:invoices"`

	ID        int64     `bun:"id,pk,autoincrement" json:"id"`
	Number    string    `bun:"number" json:"number"`
	Items     []*Item   `bun:"rel:has-many,join:id=invoice_id" json:"items,omitempty"`
	CreatedAt time.Time `bun:"created_at,nullzero,notnull,default:current_timestamp" json:"created_at"`
	UpdatedAt time.Time `bun:"updated_at,nullzero,notnull,default:current_timestamp" json:"updated_at"`
}
```

The repository uses `orm.Repository[T]` (Find, First, Get, Count, Exists,
Paginate, Create, CreateMany, Update, Delete, ForceDelete, Restore) with scopes
(`orm.Where`, `orm.OrderBy`, `orm.Limit`, `orm.With` for relations, ...), and
returns the domain's own `ErrNotFound`:

```go
invoice, err := r.rows.Find(ctx, id, orm.With("Items"), orm.With("Items.Statuses"))
return invoice, orm.MapNotFound(err, ErrNotFound)
```

Anything else is plain bun: `r.rows.Select(&dest)` or `r.rows.DB().NewSelect()`.
`internal/platform/database/orm` imports only bun, pgx and the standard
library, so it can become a module of its own. To add a column, add a field
and the column. The project creates no tables: make them yourself, or with the
migration tool you choose (goose, golang-migrate, Atlas, ...).
{{- end}}

## Generate more

`./gortisan` (`gortisan.bat` or `.\gortisan.ps1` on Windows) runs the gortisan
version this project was created with, through `go run`. It is not a dependency:
no code imports it and `go.mod` does not list it.

```bash
./gortisan list                                   # every command and flag
{{- if .Postgres}}
./gortisan make:model user                        # internal/domain/user
./gortisan make:model sales/order                 # a grouped subject
{{- end}}
./gortisan make:service user                      # internal/domain/user/service.go
./gortisan make:handler v1/user/list              # internal/api/v1/users: handler + ListRequest + ListResponse
./gortisan make:handler v2/user/list              # a second API version
./gortisan make:enum user/status --members "active,blocked"
./gortisan make:validator address/mobile
./gortisan make:middleware request_id
./gortisan make:client payment
{{- if .Redis}}
./gortisan make:cache user/profile --type "*User"
{{- end}}

```
